:: Start
<<goto "Beginning">>


:: Beginning [beginning]
<<silently>>
<<set $redStone = false>>
<<set $blueStone = false>>
<<set $greenStone = false>>
<<set $limeStone = false>>
<<set $purpleStone = false>>
<<set $stoneCount = 0>>
<</silently>>
You wake up in a field.

Your sleep was amazing.

Life is good.

[[stay = You could stay here forever.|NeutralEnding]]

[[getUp = Or you can get up...|GetUp]]


:: GetUp [beginning]
You get up and begin walking to see what the world has to offer.

The field goes on for a very long time.

You are unsure if you will ever encounter something new and meaningful.

Should you have went back to sleep?

Would life have been easier?

[[keepMoving = Keep moving|Entrance]]


:: Entrance [entrance]
Finally, you come across a structure.

It's a door.

No other walls connecting to it. Nothing else surrounding it.

It doesn't appear to be locked.

You also notice a sign next to the door with a [[disclaimer = disclaimer|disclaimer]]. Thats really weird.

[[enter = Enter?|MazeStart]]

[[leave = Leave, and go back to rest.|NeutralEnding]]


:: disclaimer
Entering this door could result in the following:

- Headaches
- Nausea
- Loss of sanity
- Lifespan decreased
- Hatred
- Pain

It is highly recommended to use an external tool (pen and paper or spreadsheet) to track progress.

[[enter = Enter?|MazeStart]]

[[leave = Leave, and go back to rest.|NeutralEnding]]


:: NeutralEnding [ending]
The End

You decide to remain in the field.

Life is good.

Why make it worse?

You close your eyes and go back to sleep...


:: MazeStart [maze]
You go through the wooden door.

You hear it slam behind you.

When you turn around to look at it, it's gone.

The room you are in is dimly lit, it's cold.

This big room was not visible from outside.

[[hiddenContinue = :(|Maze]]


:: Maze [maze]
The room is cold.


:: StonePickup [maze]
<<set $stoneCount = $stoneCount + 1>>
The stone glows faintly in your hand.


:: Teleport [maze]
A thick layer of mist surrounds you for a moment. As it clears, you see a stand with a compass on it in the middle of the room, pointing north.


:: Compass [maze]
In the middle of the room is a stand with a compass on it, pointing north.


:: Altar [maze]
An altar stands here, with five hollows carved into its surface.

<<if $stoneCount >= 0>>
[[placeStones = Place the stones on the altar|Ending]]
<<else>>
You only have $stoneCount of 5 stones. Something is still missing.
<<endif>>


:: Ending [ending]
You place each of the stones into the altar.

Once they are all slotted, they begin to glow.

You feel a rumbling underneath you as the part of the ground you are standing on begins to lift.

When you look up you, you see nothing, how long will you go up for?

Was all of this worth it?

True Ending

Thank you for playing.
